# First Aid case coverage (mandatory)

Every case must **touch the high-yield First Aid material** for its presentation — not just the single diagnosis paragraph. Steve studies from First Aid; the sim case should be a **guided tour** through every relevant index hit for that concern.

## Golden rule

**Search First Aid first → map every hit → wire into the case → then promote.**

| Step | What |
|------|------|
| 1 | **Search** local index for presentation + concern + differential branches |
| 2 | **List** all distinct book pages / topics (coverage map table) |
| 3 | **Assign** each row to HPI, exam, stack, result, tutor beat, or bibliography link |
| 4 | **Promote** only when primary rows are touched (deferred rows need explicit reason) |

Attendant voice still wins on clinical dilemmas; First Aid coverage wins on **completeness** — don't skip a classic mimic if FA teaches it for this complaint.

## When to run

| Phase | Action |
|-------|--------|
| **Capture** (`docs/cases/case-NNN-*.md`) | Run coverage script; paste table into markdown |
| **Before promote** | Fill **Touch in this case** column; add missing stacks if gaps |
| **Bibliography UI** | Link rows with `pdfPage1` from `page-map.json` (not book page in browser URL) |

Pairs with `attendant-case-canon.mdc` Phase 2b — First Aid is **step 1** of enrichment, PubMed/guidelines step 2.

## Search workflow (agents)

**Cwd:** `C:\Users\steve\MeWorld\game`

### 1. Build term list from the case

Start from:

- CCS **title** / presentation key (e.g. `Dysphagia`, `Dyspareunia`)
- **Chief complaint** + diagnosis + attendant differential rows
- **Mechanism branches** (e.g. dysphagia → achalasia, GERD, cancer, Zenker, epiglottitis, LA enlargement)

Aim for **8–20 search terms** — broad enough to catch all FA instances, not one keyword only.

### 2. Run coverage script (preferred)

```powershell
cd C:\Users\steve\MeWorld\game
python scripts/first-aid-case-coverage.py --case-id 097 `
  --terms "dyspareunia,menopause,atrophic vaginitis,GSM,prolactin,FSH,estradiol,TSH,osteoporosis,DEXA"
```

Paste stdout into `docs/cases/case-NNN-*.md` under **First Aid coverage map**.

### 3. Single-term probes (optional)

```powershell
python scripts/build-first-aid-index.py --search "dysphagia"
python scripts/build-first-aid-index.py --topic "Menopause"
```

Requires `reference/first-aid/index/pages.json` (run `npm run build:first-aid-index` once if missing).

### 4. Fill the coverage table

For each row, set **Touch in this case** to one of:

| Touch type | Example |
|------------|---------|
| HPI pivot | "12 mo amenorrhea" |
| Exam | "Pale atrophic mucosa" |
| Stack | `fsh-estradiol`, pelvic exam |
| Result text | FSH 68, E2 8 |
| Tutor beat | Prolactinoma mimic in differential table |
| Bibliography | `caseBibliography.js` → FA p.653 / pdfPage1 674 |
| **deferred** | "Not this vignette — cite in tutor only if asked" |

**Bar:** Every **primary** FA page for the chief concern must have a touch. Secondary pages (e.g. Sjögren dyspareunia on 474 when case is GSM) → tutor differential or deferred with reason.

## Example — Dysphagia case

Search terms: `dysphagia, achalasia, GERD, esophageal cancer, Zenker, epiglottitis, aspiration, botulism, mitral stenosis, Plummer-Vinson`

FA hits include book p.383–385 (achalasia, GERD, cancer), p.391 (Zenker), p.288 (LA compression), p.182 (epiglottitis), p.136 (botulism) — case should **reach** each through story, order, or explicit tutor branch.

## Example — Dyspareunia / GSM (097)

Primary touches (minimum):

| FA p. | Topic | Touch |
|-------|-------|-------|
| 653 / PDF 674 | Menopause definition | HPI amenorrhea ≥12 mo |
| 334 / 355 | Prolactin | Differential mimic |
| 331–332 | FSH/LH/GnRH | Lab results |
| 467+ | Osteoporosis / bone | DEXA stack |
| 661 | Lichen / atrophic | Exam overlap in tutor |

